[19, "o", "\r\npartition_cap: The deployment is fully ready at 4/4, and scaling is capped by Kafka partition count rather than pod readiness. The ScaledObject, HPA, and Deployment all match for demo/orders-worker; HPA desired is 4 within bounds and equals Deployment desired/ready. Kafka shows the exact same cluster/topic/consumer group with 4 partitions and lag 800, while the external metric for demo/orders/s0-kafka-orders is 400. With threshold 100, lag // target = 8 > 4, but the measured total external metric equals 4*100, which is consistent with classic KEDA Kafka plain-lag scaling being capped at one active consumer per partition.\r\n"]
